# A loop calls the function, so it is hot, and the two blocks that end in a throw are rare. The likely way is two comparisons, an addition and the return.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="checkBoth" role=Source
# CHECK: Double b@[[first]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[firstIsNegative]] = LessThan(b@[[first]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[firstIsNegative]], Terminal,
# CHECK: Double b@[[second]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[secondIsNegative]] = LessThan(b@[[second]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[secondIsNegative]], Terminal,
# CHECK: Double b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[first]], b@[[second]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[sum]], Terminal)
# What the rare blocks do in front of the throw is the same but for the number, so it is moved into one shared body. Each block is a direct call of it, with the number unboxed in a register, and the throw.
# CHECK: BB#{{*}}: ; frequency = 0.00
# CHECK: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[second]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = WarmAny, {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: :ThrowNewError)
# CHECK: BB#{{*}}: ; frequency = 0.00
# CHECK: Void b@{{*}} = Patchpoint(b@[[first]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = WarmAny, {{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: :ThrowNewError)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The reads by name, the call by value and the boxing of the number are in the shared body alone.
# NONE-LABEL: name="checkBoth" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: Patchpoint(
# NONE: Return(
# NONE-NOT: :PropGet)
# NONE-NOT: :Call)
# NONE-NOT: BitwiseCast(
# NONE-NOT: Reads:ModuleVariables
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS-LABEL: f1: size=
# CALLS-NEXT: function [[body]] x2
# CALLS: [[body]]: size=
# CALLS: stub CallValue
# X64: instructions: 5, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: 7
# ARM64: instructions: 4, patchpoints: 0, rare instructions: 7
